  "playbook": {
    "rules": 3,
    "examples": 6,
    "chars": 1362,
    "text": "House rules, learned from labelled examples:\n- Model confuses feature requests or general praise (feedback) with specific product inquiries due to overlapping language about features. These go to feedback, not product_question.\n- Model incorrectly assigns billing queries to shipping when text includes both payment and delivery terms, failing to prioritize intent. These go to billing, not shipping.\n- Model mislabels shipping-related issues as billing when text mentions payment or charges alongside delivery, due to weak contextual disambiguation. These go to shipping, not billing.\n\nWorked examples:\nTicket: Love the new dark theme, it's so easy on the eyes during late night sessions!\nLabel: feedback\nTicket: The search speed improvement in v3.2 is noticeable, great work on that optimization.\nLabel: feedback\nTicket: I was charged twice for my Pro subscription this month. Can you look into the duplicate charge on my latest invoice?\nLabel: billing\nTicket: The starter kit arrived quickly and the packaging was lovely, but I still need a corrected receipt for the charge on my credit card.\nLabel: billing\nTicket: The physical notebook I ordered hasn't arrived yet. Tracking number LN-8822 shows no updates since last week.\nLabel: shipping\nTicket: My starter kit shipment was delayed and the box arrived damaged. I'd like a replacement sent.\nLabel: shipping"
  },
